# THE TICKET'S OWN REPRO, and the one row that is not hermetic -- see the
# Makefile, which SKIPS it loudly when this box has no GL headers.
#
# `/usr/include/GL/gl.h` has the file stem `gl` and the library is `libGL.so.1`:
# the capitals live in the DIRECTORY, which the resolver discards before anything
# looks at it, so an exact /etc/ld.so.cache lookup asks a question the host
# cannot answer and the compiler emitted `libgl.so` -- a green build, dead at
# exec. Written with the RELATIVE spelling, which needed the include-path
# fallback to resolve at all, so this row exercises both halves of the group at
# once.
import "GL/gl.h"
print(glGetError())
